  "about": "The kinds of monster. Read by js/world.js. Their letter and name; how they fight and move; their ways.",
  "fields": {
    "glyph": "the letter drawn",
    "name": "its name",
    "speed": "moves for each of the player's",
    "wander": "how much it wanders when milling about (the goblins' 1)",
    "pack": "how many to a pack [least, most]",
    "crypt": "how many to a pack in a crypt",
    "hp": "hit points [least, most]",
    "hit": "the chance its blow hits",
    "dmg": "its blow's damage [least, most]",
    "verb": "what its blow is called",
    "bleeds": "a hard blow of its makes the player bleed",
    "poison": "the chance its blow poisons",
    "xp": "experience for a kill",
    "undead": "never flees",
    "drops": "sometimes drops what it carried",
    "erratic": "flits about, even chasing",
    "lurker": "waits still till roused",
    "relentless": "never gives up a chase",
    "patrol": "its pack walks from room to room",
    "lantern": "carries a lantern: lights the player near it",
    "regen": "heals, hit points a turn",
    "boss": "killing it wins",
    "vision": "how well it sees what's in light: clear, kind, faint, whole steps reaching half a step more; seeing the player clearly or their kind, it sees them, faint a glimpse; in dim light none clear and each halved (null: none, the light-shy) (spec/light-rebuild.md, S4)",
    "dark": "how well it sees in the dark, the same three: from itself, or (not the light-shy) from a lit or dim square it sees, but past a light no better than its vision would see it lit",
    "lightShy": "sees by its dark vision alone; a band worse on a dim square, two on a lit one; a light's own square stops its sight as rock does"
  },
